// An east const (`int const x`) qualifies the object as a leading one does
// (declarator_written_cv's base_const), so the write is refused. g++ 13
// (-std=c++17): "assignment of read-only variable 'x'"; clang++ 18: "cannot
// assign to variable 'x' with const-qualified type 'const int'". Before the
// fix madc compiled it and the program returned 2.
int main() { int const x = 1; x = 2; return x; }
